WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.203 --> 00:00:02.735
-Thank you so much for
coming back and being here.

00:00:02.735 --> 00:00:06.272
I do want to get into your tour,
"Patton Oswalt Live."

00:00:06.272 --> 00:00:07.439
If you want to see
a great comedian,

00:00:07.439 --> 00:00:08.808
please check out Patton Oswalt.

00:00:08.808 --> 00:00:13.613
You're doing Friday, September
17th, Washington, D.C.,

00:00:13.613 --> 00:00:15.648
at the Kennedy Center
Concert Hall.

00:00:15.648 --> 00:00:17.217
Two shows.
That's a big jam right there.

00:00:17.217 --> 00:00:19.618
-Yeah.
-On the 18th at Virginia Beach

00:00:19.618 --> 00:00:21.521
at Sandler Center
for Performing Arts.

00:00:21.521 --> 00:00:23.589
You got like 20 dates on here.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:00:23.589 --> 00:00:25.191
It's been amazing. It's been --

00:00:25.191 --> 00:00:28.127
I'm in front of
live audiences again,

00:00:28.127 --> 00:00:30.963
and it's great enough
to be, like, hearing --

00:00:30.963 --> 00:00:34.767
like, I'm so used to being
inside, so it's all emojis

00:00:34.767 --> 00:00:36.135
and thumbs-up over the Internet

00:00:36.135 --> 00:00:37.803
when I'm tweeting
or texting someone.

00:00:37.803 --> 00:00:40.173
And now I'm like, "What's that
noise coming out --

00:00:40.173 --> 00:00:42.075
Oh, that's laughter. Oh, yeah.
That's laughter."

00:00:42.075 --> 00:00:46.312
[ Cheers and applause ]
"Oh, okay, okay, okay, okay."

00:00:46.312 --> 00:00:48.748
-I was scared.
-But what's weird is

00:00:48.748 --> 00:00:51.517
a lot of times it's entertaining
not even for the laughter.

00:00:51.517 --> 00:00:53.953
It feels like me and the
audience are checking in

00:00:53.953 --> 00:00:55.922
with each other just to confirm

00:00:55.922 --> 00:00:57.957
that none of us
has gone completely crazy.

00:00:57.957 --> 00:00:59.426
So when I'm on stage and go,

00:00:59.426 --> 00:01:01.594
"So I had, like,
Doritos for breakfast,"

00:01:01.594 --> 00:01:03.095
and they're like,
"We had Doritos!"

00:01:03.095 --> 00:01:04.296
Okay, good. We didn't go crazy.

00:01:04.296 --> 00:01:05.698
Good, we're all
on the same page."

00:01:05.698 --> 00:01:07.666
-Did you pour Pepsi over yours?

00:01:07.666 --> 00:01:10.769
-Okay, good, yeah, great, I kind
of went crazy for a little.

00:01:10.769 --> 00:01:14.107
So we all are confirming that
our minds broke

00:01:14.107 --> 00:01:15.608
during quarantine
and during the shutdowns.

00:01:15.608 --> 00:01:21.881
-I know you got in some news,
some headlines, last two weeks

00:01:21.881 --> 00:01:23.883
or something like that because
you had to cancel some shows.

00:01:23.883 --> 00:01:28.754
-I canceled some shows
because the venues --

00:01:28.754 --> 00:01:30.656
It wasn't really
the venues' fault.

00:01:30.656 --> 00:01:32.859
There were four shows in Florida
that unfortunately right now

00:01:32.859 --> 00:01:36.495
they don't let these venues
enforce COVID protocols because

00:01:36.495 --> 00:01:37.830
it's against the law for them.

00:01:37.830 --> 00:01:40.632
And then there was another gig
in Salt Lake City.

00:01:40.632 --> 00:01:42.768
I had to cancel
and it killed me.

00:01:42.768 --> 00:01:45.237
I love going to Florida.
It would have been in December.

00:01:45.237 --> 00:01:49.242
And then I -- But then I started
getting all this weird push.

00:01:49.242 --> 00:01:51.778
90% of the feedback
was very positive.

00:01:51.778 --> 00:01:54.447
"Thank you, we'll see you in the
future when things are saner."

00:01:54.447 --> 00:01:57.283
I did get the even split between

00:01:57.283 --> 00:02:00.887
"You're a Nazi for demanding
the cards," 'cause, yeah,

00:02:00.887 --> 00:02:03.022
that was Hitler's big thing,

00:02:03.022 --> 00:02:05.057
was making sure
that no one was vaccinated.

00:02:05.057 --> 00:02:08.360
[ Laughter ]
And then also, but I also got --

00:02:08.360 --> 00:02:10.462
-Was that his big thing?
-That was his big thing.

00:02:10.462 --> 00:02:12.365
"Hey, don't get the --"
-That's right. You're right.

00:02:12.365 --> 00:02:14.500
-"Listen to me. Horse paste.

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:16.469
Make sure they use
the horse paste."

00:02:16.469 --> 00:02:19.238
And then the other one --
-Horse paste.

00:02:19.238 --> 00:02:23.075
-I either get that or I get
the "You're a pussy."

00:02:23.075 --> 00:02:27.580
And I was like, "Why -- When did
everyone become Thanos

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:30.149
where it's just like,
'Whoever dies, dies.

00:02:30.149 --> 00:02:31.750
Just go out there.'"

00:02:31.750 --> 00:02:35.722
And by the way, if that is your
philosophy, don't die for a --

00:02:35.722 --> 00:02:38.624
Go die seeing Lizzo.
Like, that's a good...

00:02:38.624 --> 00:02:40.293
[ Laughter and applause ]
...last concert to see.

00:02:40.293 --> 00:02:43.062
-Wait, no, no, no!
You shouldn't die!

00:02:43.062 --> 00:02:44.764
-By the way, you shouldn't die
for any entertainer.

00:02:44.764 --> 00:02:46.465
But if you are, make it count.
-Not you.

00:02:46.465 --> 00:02:49.569
-Don't be in the hospital going,
"I'm so glad I got to see

00:02:49.569 --> 00:02:52.238
that fat nerd whine about
'The Mandalorian.'"

00:02:52.238 --> 00:02:54.340
[ Imitates flatline ]
[ Laughter ]

00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:59.979
That's a terrible final -- That
shouldn't be your last thing!

00:02:59.979 --> 00:03:02.048
Don't roll the dice
for that stuff.

00:03:02.048 --> 00:03:03.382
[ Laughter ]

00:03:03.382 --> 00:03:06.286
-If you want to laugh safely,
please go see Patton.

00:03:06.286 --> 00:03:08.221
I want to talk about "A.P. Bio."

00:03:08.221 --> 00:03:10.689
Season 4 now is on Peacock.

00:03:10.689 --> 00:03:13.926
And one of your costars
is one of my old pals,

00:03:13.926 --> 00:03:16.395
my old favorites, one of
the funniest humans, Paula Pell.

00:03:16.395 --> 00:03:21.534
-Paula Pell is such a -- She was
already a force as a writer.

00:03:21.534 --> 00:03:23.168
Now she's acting on the show.

00:03:23.168 --> 00:03:25.804
There are so many scenes
where they were shooting

00:03:25.804 --> 00:03:27.640
over my shoulder
and I would blow the scene.

00:03:27.640 --> 00:03:30.276
There's one scene in the first
episode where she describes

00:03:30.276 --> 00:03:33.545
her grandfathers being killed by
a tornado,

00:03:33.545 --> 00:03:35.381
and she describes it like --
I think it's

00:03:35.381 --> 00:03:38.985
two balloons full of SpaghettiOs
in the air.

00:03:38.985 --> 00:03:41.654
And I'm laughing so hard,
I blew so many takes

00:03:41.654 --> 00:03:43.122
because my shoulders
were going up and down.

00:03:43.122 --> 00:03:45.658
I'm like hunched over laughing,
and they're like, "No, no,

00:03:45.658 --> 00:03:47.760
she's telling you a serious --
You can't be laughing at her..."

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:49.128
-She's unbelievable.
-"...because it makes you

00:03:49.128 --> 00:03:50.696
look like a psychopath."

00:03:50.696 --> 00:03:53.232
And so many things
that you loved on "SNL,"

00:03:53.232 --> 00:03:55.334
she was the brains behind.

00:03:55.334 --> 00:03:57.169
-I want to show a clip.

00:03:57.169 --> 00:04:01.207
Here's Patton Oswalt and Paula
Pell in Season 4 of "A.P. Bio."

00:04:01.207 --> 00:04:02.742
Take a look at this.

00:04:02.742 --> 00:04:04.744
-Mama, it's Ralph.

00:04:04.744 --> 00:04:07.746
I want to thank you for treating
me like a second-class citizen.

00:04:07.746 --> 00:04:10.282
I became stronger
because I had to be!

00:04:10.282 --> 00:04:11.684
You messed me up!

00:04:11.684 --> 00:04:13.586
Thank you!

00:04:13.586 --> 00:04:16.589
-[ Clapping ]

00:04:16.589 --> 00:04:19.958
Ralph Durbin,
you're a goddamn tiger.

00:04:19.958 --> 00:04:23.029
-[ Roars ]

00:04:23.029 --> 00:04:27.700
-Now you're ready.

00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:29.969
-Hello, Don? Yeah, it's Ralph.

00:04:29.969 --> 00:04:32.238
Listen, those price hikes,

00:04:32.238 --> 00:04:33.939
they're not going to
work for me, bud.

00:04:33.939 --> 00:04:36.843
I'm not paying a penny more
for those tots.

00:04:36.843 --> 00:04:38.578
Good. Good.

00:04:38.578 --> 00:04:40.512
I'm glad you see it my way.

00:04:40.512 --> 00:04:43.082
Oh, Daphne says hi?

00:04:43.082 --> 00:04:46.752
Well, you can tell your wife
to kiss my ass!

00:04:46.752 --> 00:04:48.253
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:48.253 --> 00:04:49.521
-No!

00:04:49.521 --> 00:04:51.724
Patton Oswalt, everybody

00:04:51.724 --> 00:04:56.062
Season 4 of "A.P. Bio" is
streaming now on Peacock,

00:04:56.062 --> 00:04:58.765
and you can check him out
live on tour.

